From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] local: pmdomain: core: drop default performance-state votes across system suspend

genpd applies a device's "required-opps" as its default performance state at
attach time. That vote is dropped by genpd_runtime_suspend() and restored by
genpd_runtime_resume(), but genpd_finish_suspend() does not touch it, so a
device that is never runtime-suspended keeps voting its full operating corner
on the parent rail for the whole of a system suspend.

On the Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x (X1E-80-100) that is five devices: the three dwc3
controllers and both PCIe root complexes, each carrying
required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom>, all with runtime_status=active for the life
of the boot. Tracing rpmh:rpmh_send_msg across an s2idle shows the consequence
directly: cx.lvl is written exactly once at boot, to index 5 (vlvl 256,
NOMINAL), and never again -- not in the suspend path, not in the sleep set. The
CX rail sits at NOMINAL through every suspend while the devices that asked for
it have their rails and clocks off. pcie-qcom drops its OPP in suspend_noirq on
the operating-points-v2 path; the required-opps path gets nothing.

Drop the vote in the noirq suspend phase, where runtime PM would have dropped
it, and restore it in the noirq resume phase before the domain is powered
back on -- the same ordering as genpd_runtime_resume(). rpmhpd floors an
enabled domain at its enable corner, so on this machine CX goes from 256 to
16 (RETENTION) while its child GDSCs still hold it on.

Off by default. pmdomain.drop_pstate_on_suspend=1 on the kernel command line
enables it for a boot; /sys/module/pmdomain/parameters/drop_pstate_on_suspend
and /sys/kernel/debug/pm_genpd/drop_pstate_on_suspend switch it at runtime,
effective from the next suspend, so one build gives both A/B arms. The module
parameter carries an explicit "pmdomain." prefix because the file's
KBUILD_MODNAME is "core".

--- a/include/linux/pm_domain.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
@@ -292,6 +292,7 @@
 	unsigned int performance_state;
 	unsigned int default_pstate;
 	unsigned int rpm_pstate;
+	unsigned int sys_pstate;
 	unsigned int opp_token;
 	bool hw_mode;
 	bool rpm_always_on;
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <linux/export.h>
 #include <linux/cpu.h>
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 
 /* Provides a unique ID for each genpd device */
 static DEFINE_IDA(genpd_ida);
@@ -276,6 +277,25 @@
 	smp_mb__after_atomic();
 }
 
+/*
+ * A device's default performance state (its "required-opps") is dropped when it
+ * runtime-suspends and restored when it runtime-resumes, but nothing touches it
+ * across system suspend. A device that is never runtime-suspended therefore
+ * keeps voting its full operating corner on the parent rail through the whole
+ * suspend. Drop those votes in the noirq suspend phase, mirroring the runtime PM
+ * behaviour, and restore them on resume. Off unless pmdomain.drop_pstate_on_suspend=1
+ * is on the command line; /sys/module/pmdomain/parameters/ and
+ * /sys/kernel/debug/pm_genpd/drop_pstate_on_suspend switch it at runtime, from
+ * the next suspend on. The prefix override keeps it off KBUILD_MODNAME "core".
+ */
+static bool genpd_drop_pstate_on_suspend;
+
+#undef MODULE_PARAM_PREFIX
+#define MODULE_PARAM_PREFIX "pmdomain."
+module_param_named(drop_pstate_on_suspend, genpd_drop_pstate_on_suspend, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(drop_pstate_on_suspend,
+		 "Drop default performance-state votes across system suspend (default 0)");
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
 static struct dentry *genpd_debugfs_dir;
 
@@ -1542,6 +1562,7 @@
 				int (*suspend_noirq)(struct device *dev),
 				int (*resume_noirq)(struct device *dev))
 {
+	struct generic_pm_domain_data *gpd_data = dev_gpd_data(dev);
 	struct generic_pm_domain *genpd;
 	int ret = 0;
 
@@ -1567,6 +1588,8 @@
 	}
 
 	genpd_lock(genpd);
+	if (genpd_drop_pstate_on_suspend)
+		gpd_data->sys_pstate = genpd_drop_performance_state(dev);
 	genpd->suspended_count++;
 	genpd_sync_power_off(genpd, true, 0);
 	genpd_unlock(genpd);
@@ -1600,6 +1623,7 @@
 static int genpd_finish_resume(struct device *dev,
 			       int (*resume_noirq)(struct device *dev))
 {
+	struct generic_pm_domain_data *gpd_data = dev_gpd_data(dev);
 	struct generic_pm_domain *genpd;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -1614,6 +1638,8 @@
 		return resume_noirq(dev);
 
 	genpd_lock(genpd);
+	genpd_restore_performance_state(dev, gpd_data->sys_pstate);
+	gpd_data->sys_pstate = 0;
 	genpd_sync_power_on(genpd, true, 0);
 	genpd->suspended_count--;
 	genpd_unlock(genpd);
@@ -4144,6 +4170,8 @@
 
 	debugfs_create_file("pm_genpd_summary", S_IRUGO, genpd_debugfs_dir,
 			    NULL, &summary_fops);
+	debugfs_create_bool("drop_pstate_on_suspend", 0644, genpd_debugfs_dir,
+			    &genpd_drop_pstate_on_suspend);
 
 	list_for_each_entry(genpd, &gpd_list, gpd_list_node)
 		genpd_debug_add(genpd);
